      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-342494",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}+x(2x-3){y}^{\u2032}-3y=0\n$$\n\nThe general solution near $x=0$ of the differential equation above is given by\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{3}{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(3){x}^{n}+{c}_{2}{y}_{2}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ are arbitrary constants and ${a}_{n}(\\lambda )$ are coefficients dependent on $\\lambda $ (solutions of the indicial equation) and determined by substitution.\nWhich of the following is the form of the second Frobenius solution ${y}_{2}?$\n\n*Hint: You may assume $x=0$ is a regular singular point of the ODE and the indicial equation of the ODE is $2{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -3=0.$*"
